  "checks": [
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.sqPair: E:spatial-physical-pair",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:108-109 defines 'pairing Γ (fun x => ofReal (f x ^ 2)) (fun x => ofReal (h x ^ 2))', without hypotheses. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:15-19 defines 'B_Γ(f,h)=∫ f(x)h(x-y)ν(dx,dy)' initially as an extended nonnegative integral. Specialization to squares is exact; ledger:3171 and claims.yaml:11471 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.gradSqE: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:114 defines '∫⁻ x, ‖gf x‖ₑ ^ 2', without asserting gf is a gradient. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:35 defines 'b(g)=‖∇g‖_2^2' on H^1. Ledger:3172 and claims.yaml:11478 correctly condition the identification on gf being a weak gradient; the unlabelled mapping is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.Nnorm: P:spatial-four-linear",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:119-120 uses 'sqrt (∫ f²) ^ (1-alpha/4) * sqrt (∫ ‖gf‖²) ^ (alpha/4)'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:151-152 has 'f ∈ H^1' and 'N(f)=‖f‖_2^{1-alpha/4}‖∇f‖_2^{alpha/4}'. On the stated L^2 weak-gradient interpretation these coincide. Ledger:3173 and claims.yaml:11485 accurately expose the Bochner formulation."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.SquarePairingBounds: P:spatial-four-linear",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:133-139 requires 'MemLp f 2', 'MemLp gf 2', 'HasWeakGradient f gf', and similarly for h, supplying the diagonal bound and squared square-pairing CS. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:151-157 assumes real H^1 profiles and states 'A_sp(f) ≤ R_0 N(f)^4' and 'B_Γ(f²,h²) ≤ sqrt(A_sp(f)A_sp(h))'. Finiteness makes the formulations equivalent at R=R_0. Ledger:3174 and claims.yaml:11492 match; discharge is explicit at SpatialOccupationL7Completed.lean:253-266,310-313."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.Tlin: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:142 defines '∫⁻ s, gradSqE (DG s) ∂volI'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:312-313 defines 'T(g)=∫_0^1 b(g_s) ds < infinity' for the occupation class. The nonnegative extended formulation agrees on admissible fields; ledger:3175 and claims.yaml:11499 state it accurately."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.IsOccField: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:154-158 requires 'AEStronglyMeasurable' joint G and DG, '∀ᵐ s, IsUnitH1 (G s) (DG s)', and 'Tlin DG < top'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:311-314 requires 'strongly H^1-measurable fields', unit norm a.e., and finite T. Ledger:3098-3107,3176 explicitly records the unformalized identification in both directions; claims.yaml:11506 accurately describes the model. No additional time smoothness or support restriction is hidden. Acceptance concerns this disclosed representative-based scope, not an asserted formal equivalence of classes."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.Jlin: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:164-165 defines '∫⁻ s, ∫⁻ t, ofReal (Kstar a D (s-t)) * sqPair Γ (G s) (G t)'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:321-323 defines the same nonnegative double integral; its proof:358 explicitly permits positive Tonelli before finiteness. Ledger:3090-3093 specifies inner t and outer s, resolving the abbreviated wording at ledger:3177 and claims.yaml:11513."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.J: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:504 defines '(Jlin a D Γ G).toReal'; finiteness under the analytic hypotheses and IsOccField is proved at :530-577. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:324-327 states 'every g ∈ O' satisfies '0 ≤ J(g) ≤ ... < infinity'. Ledger:3178 and claims.yaml:11520 correctly attach the finiteness qualification rather than treating unrestricted toReal as an integral."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.T: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:507 defines '(Tlin DG).toReal', with 'energy_lt_top : Tlin DG < top' in IsOccField at :158. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:312-313 requires 'T(g)=∫_0^1 b(g_s) ds < infinity'. Ledger:3179 and claims.yaml:11527 agree; T_eq_integral supplies the real-integral identification."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.spEnergyVal: E:spatial-energy-map",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:582-583 defines '(2-alpha)/2 * alpha^(alpha/(2-alpha)) * R^(2/(2-alpha))', without hypotheses. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:239-244 gives that formula at R_sp under the standing assumptions. Ledger:3180 and claims.yaml:11534 explicitly map only the right-hand formula at arbitrary real R, not the spatial supremum itself. All factors and exponents match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.energySet: E:occupation-own-energy",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:731-733 defines values witnessed by 'IsOccField G DG' and 'v = J ... G - T DG / 2'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:328-331 takes 'sup_{g∈O}(J(g)-T(g)/2)' over exactly its class. Ledger:3181 and claims.yaml:11541 accurately state the value set over the disclosed modelled class; the coefficient 1/2 is unchanged."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.EstarO: E:occupation-own-energy",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:737 defines 'sSup (energySet a D Γ)'; :743-765 proves 'Nonempty ∧ BddAbove' under the stated analytic assumptions. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:330-332 defines the occupation supremum, and :364-369 supplies its positive witness and finiteness. Ledger:3182 and claims.yaml:11548 correctly cite the theorem making this a genuine supremum."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.squareCS_of_sqrt: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:169-170 assumes 'X ≠ top', 'A ≠ top', 'B ≠ top', and 'X.toReal ≤ sqrt(A.toReal * B.toReal)', concluding 'X^2 ≤ A*B'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:152-157 states finite physical pairings and the real square-root bound, not this abstract conversion lemma. Ledger:3183 and claims.yaml:11555 faithfully describe a Lean-route auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.ae_prod_both: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:181-184 assumes '∀ᵐ s ∂volI, P s' and concludes the property at both coordinates product-a.e. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:358-359 says 'Null-time modifications affect only a product-null set'; it does not state this standalone predicate lemma. Ledger:3184 and claims.yaml:11562 match; the auxiliary classification is sound."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.sqPair_congr: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:189-190 assumes '[IsLocallyFiniteMeasure Γ]', 'f =ᵐ f′' and 'h =ᵐ h′', concluding equality of sqPair. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:18-30 states representative independence for B_Γ and explains null-set transfer. Ledger:3185 and claims.yaml:11569 correctly describe this squares-specialization auxiliary without claiming a separate labelled manuscript step."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.sqPair_aemeasurable: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:201-204 assumes locally finite Γ and 'AEStronglyMeasurable (fun p => G p.1 p.2) (volI.prod volume)', concluding 'AEMeasurable' pairings. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:318 says 'pairings ... are measurable'; :339-349 constructs joint versions and identifies the physical integral a.e. Ledger:3186 and claims.yaml:11576 accurately state the a.e. conclusion and representative hypothesis; ledger:3141-3143 records the different Tonelli route."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.gradSqE_eq: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:229-231 assumes 'MemLp gf 2 volume', concluding integrability of '‖gf‖²' and 'gradSqE gf = ofReal (∫ ‖gf‖²)'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:35 uses 'b(g)=‖∇g‖_2²' on H^1. Ledger:3187 and claims.yaml:11583 correctly present the extended-to-real bridge as an auxiliary, with no additional manuscript claim."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.sqPair_self_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:243-246 assumes '0 ≤ R', '0 ≤ alpha', SquarePairingBounds and 'IsUnitH1 f gf', yielding 'sqPair Γ f f ≤ ofReal R * gradSqE gf^(alpha/2)'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:151-154 gives the homogeneous bound and :312 imposes unit norm. Ledger:3188 and claims.yaml:11590 exactly describe the normalized specialization; its auxiliary classification and discharged input are explicit."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.sqPair_le_half: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:263-267 assumes nonnegative R and alpha, SquarePairingBounds and two unit H^1 pairs, yielding 'ofReal (R/2) * (b_f^(alpha/2)+b_h^(alpha/2))' as upper bound. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:351-356 combines square CS with '2F(s)F(t) ≤ F(s)^2+F(t)^2'. Ledger:3189 and claims.yaml:11597 correctly describe this combined auxiliary with the factor 1/2."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.row_lintegral_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:317-319 assumes '0<a', 'a<1', '0<D', 's∈Icc 0 1' and bounds the extended row by 'ofReal (Rstar a D)'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:291-298 states the exact real row maximum on [0,1]. Ledger:3190 and claims.yaml:11604 accurately describe its extended-integral auxiliary specialization."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.col_lintegral_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:336-343 assumes '0<a<1', '0<D', 't∈Icc 0 1' and proves the extended column bound using Kstar_neg. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:356-357 says the 'column bound is the same because K_star is even'. Ledger:3191 and claims.yaml:11611 match; identifying the extended formulation as an auxiliary is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.lintegral_rpow_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:348-349 assumes 'AEMeasurable f volI', '0<p', 'p<1' and proves '∫⁻ f^p ≤ (∫⁻ f)^p'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:353-355 uses '0<alpha/2<1' and concavity for b on the unit time interval. Ledger:3192 and claims.yaml:11618 correctly describe the general Hölder auxiliary, not a literal TeX proof lemma; the probability-mass normalization is proved at Lean:359-360."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.gradSqE_aemeasurable: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:368-373 assumes joint 'AEStronglyMeasurable' DG and proves 'AEMeasurable (fun s => gradSqE (DG s)) volI'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:337 derives measurability of b from continuity of the squared gradient norm on H^1. Ledger:3193 and claims.yaml:11625 accurately describe the different representative-based auxiliary route."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.Jlin_le: E:occupation-physical-bound",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:378-382 assumes '0<a<1', '0<D', '0<alpha<2', '0≤R', SquarePairingBounds and IsOccField, without local finiteness, and proves the extended bound with 'Rstar * R * (Tlin DG).toReal^(alpha/2)'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:324-326 has 'g∈O' and 'J(g)≤R_star R_sp T(g)^(alpha/2)'. Ledger:3194 and claims.yaml:11632 accurately expose the general hypotheses and constant replacement; the paper completion restores R_sp."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.sqPair_Jlin_congr: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:467-471 assumes locally finite Γ and '∀ᵐ s, G s =ᵐ[volume] G′ s', concluding product-a.e. equality of pairings and exact equality of Jlin. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:318-319 states 'representative independent', while :345-346,358-359 addresses spatial versions and null-time changes. Ledger:3195 and claims.yaml:11639 preserve these quantifiers and conclusions."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.Tlin_congr: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:484-485 assumes '∀ᵐ s, DG s =ᵐ[volume] DG′ s' and concludes 'Tlin DG = Tlin DG′'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:312-313 defines T through the squared weak-gradient norm, without a separate lemma about named gradient versions. Ledger:3196 and claims.yaml:11646 accurately classify and summarize this auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.Tlin_unique: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:496-501 assumes a.e. 'IsUnitH1 (G s) (DG s)' and 'IsUnitH1 (G s) (DG′ s)', concluding equality of Tlin by weak-gradient uniqueness. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:311-313 treats g_s as an H^1 element and b(g_s) as intrinsic. Ledger:3197 and claims.yaml:11653 match the stronger explicit unit-pair hypotheses of this auxiliary; no manuscript theorem is falsely attributed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.T_eq_integral: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:511-512 assumes 'IsOccField G DG' and proves integrability of 's ↦ ∫ x, ‖DG s x‖²' and that its integral equals T. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:312-313 assumes finite 'T(g)=∫_0^1 b(g_s) ds'; :337-338 supplies measurability. Ledger:3198 and claims.yaml:11660 accurately describe the real-integral proof step within the disclosed class model."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.occupation_physical_bound: E:occupation-physical-bound",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:530-541 assumes '0<a<1', '0<D', '0<alpha<2', '0≤R', locally finite Γ, SquarePairingBounds and IsOccField; it proves a.e. measurability, finite Jlin, the integrable product-space real form, and '0≤J≤Rstar*R*T^(alpha/2)'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:318-326 states measurability and the same bound for g∈O with R_sp. Ledger:3199 and claims.yaml:11667 accurately expose the generalization and supplied input; no finiteness is assumed instead of proved."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.scalar_max: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:587-588 assumes '0<alpha<2', '0≤c', '0≤T' and proves 'c*T^(alpha/2)-T/2 ≤ spEnergyVal alpha c'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:361-363 maximizes the expression over 'T≥0' at c=R_star R_sp. Ledger:3200 and claims.yaml:11674 explicitly claim the upper inequality, not an attainment theorem; the AM-GM route and exact constant agree with the required upper-bound step."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.Kstar_one_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:617-618 assumes '0<a', '0<D', s,t∈(0,1), and 't≠s', concluding 'Kstar ... 1 ≤ Kstar ... (s-t)'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:289 sets 'K_star(0)=0' and :292-293 states decrease only on positive arguments. Ledger:3201 and claims.yaml:11681 retain the indispensable off-diagonal condition and correctly mark this alternative positivity-route lemma as auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.volI_univ: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:631-632 proves 'volI univ = 1', without hypotheses. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:311-313 uses time interval '(0,1)' and :353-355 invokes its unit-length concavity bound. Ledger:3202 and claims.yaml:11688 correctly describe the normalization as an unlabelled auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.exists_pos_member: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:640-645 assumes the recorded parameter ranges, nonnegative R, locally finite 'Γ≠0', SetScaling and SquarePairingBounds, and concludes '∃ G DG, IsOccField G DG ∧ 0<J-T/2'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:364-369 uses a constant-in-time dilated unit compact profile to establish the same positive witness. Ledger:3203 and claims.yaml:11695 match; the disclosed K_star(1) lower-bound route is implemented at Lean:678-727 and genuinely proves nonemptiness."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.occupation_own_energy: E:occupation-own-energy",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:743-749 assumes '0<a<1', 'D>0', '0<alpha<2', 'R≥0', locally finite nonzero scaling Γ and SquarePairingBounds; it concludes Nonempty, BddAbove, and '0<EstarO≤Rstar^(2/(2-alpha))*spEnergyVal alpha R'. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:328-332 states '0<E_star^O≤R_star^(2/(2-alpha))*E_sp'. Ledger:3204 and claims.yaml:11702 correctly expose the general formula constant; the completed wrapper identifies it with E_sp."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.OccupationPhysicalClass.occupation_physical_class_paper: P:occupation-physical-class",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:782-803 assumes 'HomogCovariance d alpha a Γ μ', 'Γ≠0', 'D=(4-alpha)-2*a', and SquarePairingBounds at R_0; its universal field clause and separate global energy clause match ledger:3205 and claims.yaml:11709. TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:4-10 supplies the covariance and parameter assumptions; :311-332 supplies O, measurability, J and energy bounds. The class-model and R_0/formula differences are explicitly recorded. SpatialOccupationL7Completed.lean:310-381 removes the supplied input and restores both R_sp and the actual spatial supremum E_sp."
    },
    {
      "claim": "PARA-OccupationPhysicalClass",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:3064-3167 accurately identifies the TeX statement, standing assumptions and proof ranges. Its object definitions, extended-to-real qualifications, class-model limitation in both directions, SquarePairingBounds discharge, and distinction between spEnergyVal and E_sp agree with the four complete Lean modules. The Hölder, Tonelli, AM-GM and K_star(1) route differences are real and disclosed. K_star(0)=0 agrees with OccupationKernelRow.lean:94-95 and TeX:289. The zero-covariance remark at TeX:374-379 is correctly excluded. No hidden optimizer or compact-support condition is imposed on general occupation fields."
    },
    {
      "claim": "LEDGER-INDEX",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "All 35 declarations occur exactly once in the Index table, at ledger:511-519, under their section-row labels; the 14 route auxiliaries are grouped under 'no direct label'. The completed wrappers are separately indexed at :541. Exact label searches across all manuscript inputs returned one definition for every label cited by the reviewed section: the spatial/occupation labels in integrated_spatial_occupation.tex and H:homog in notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex:190."
    },
    {
      "claim": "COVERAGE-ROWS",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "coverage.yaml:890-916 correctly uses 'same-assumptions' with 'conclusion: weaker' and explicitly limits the result to the joint-representative class, leaving both class-identification directions unformalized. The listed claims support measurability, representative independence, nonemptiness, positivity and the exact R_sp/E_sp bounds; no analytic input remains in the completed occupation wrappers. docs/coverage-scope-tex.yaml:28-30 has matching ASCII and TeX scope statements. This is not an unqualified claim to have formalized the strong-H^1 class identification."
    },
    {
      "claim": "CROSS-REFERENCES",
      "verdict": "PASS_WITH_NOTES",
      "reason": "Relevant cross-references at ledger:166-171,3818-3823,3891,3918,4004-4038,4056-4058,5936-5956 consistently describe input discharge, exact constants and the remaining class-model limitation. The 'Not in Lean' list correctly retains strong-H^1 measurability/class identification, the exact J_0 calculation and the zero-covariance remark. Only the generic source-path wording in Scope:29-30 needs an optional clarification; the correct whole-result path is already given at :250-253."
    }
  ],
  "findings": {
    "fatal": [],
    "major": [],
    "minor": [
      "W1 — Scope source-path wording: candidate/statement-ledger.md:29-30 says 'The exact statement is the Lean type in StratonovichHAMAudit/<Module>.lean', although these whole-result declarations are in StratonovichHAMSecondMoment; for example OccupationPhysicalClass.lean:108-109 defines 'sqPair ... := pairing Γ ...', corresponding to TeX integrated_spatial_occupation.tex:15-19, 'B_Γ(f,h)=∫ f(x)h(x-y)ν(dx,dy)'. The correct distinction already appears at ledger:250-253, so this is nonblocking. Optional fix: mention both source namespaces in Scope:29-30 or refer there to the later path distinction."
    ]
  },
  "required_repairs": [],
  "limitations": [
    "Acceptance is limited to the ledger's explicitly disclosed representative-based occupation model. Neither direction of its formal identification with strongly H^1-measurable fields is proved in the packet.",
    "Requirement A was completed. Partial-file coverage outside its required sections and declarations reflects the expressly limited review scope; unrelated ledger rows and unrelated module contents were not reviewed.",
    "Compilation, absence of sorry and the standard-axiom restriction were accepted as supplied; no build was run. Supervisor-checked byte binding was not independently recomputed.",
    "This AI correspondence review is not human verification, a novelty audit, or verification of the manuscript's remaining stochastic results."
  ]
}
